  "query_preview": "..\nA moderately drier trade-wind pattern will continue across the\nMarianas the next several days, with a chance for a shower or two to\nmake its way across Guam and Rota overnight. Winds will begin to\npickup beginning Saturday, followed by an arrival of a broad trade-\nwind trough that is expected to bring low-end scattered showers early\nnext week. Winds will remain elevated for the rest of the forecast\nperiod as the high off the coast of Japan continues its trek east and\nincreasing pressure gradients with the tropics.",
